camchrome: a Windows persona shows regional-indicator pairs as letters, as Segoe UI Emoji does.

Clearcote audit, Windows persona on a Linux host: "flag pair / two letters = 0.500 ... a
regional-indicator pair ligated into one flag. Windows' Segoe UI Emoji has no flag glyphs, so this
emoji font came from another OS." Noto Color Emoji forms flags through its ccmp feature, which
also forms ZWJ and skin-tone sequences that Segoe UI Emoji supports. Under a Windows persona the
shaper turns ccmp off at regional-indicator code points only (a range-limited HarfBuzz feature),
so a pair renders as two letters while every other emoji sequence still shapes.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/shaping/harfbuzz_shaper.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/shaping/harfbuzz_shaper.cc
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
